      "description": "Turns threaded DPCs back on if a tweak tool turned them off. Microsoft documents that they then run as ordinary DPCs, each of which increases system latency and can hurt audio and video playback. This undoes a tweak; it is not a performance setting, and no frame-rate effect is claimed.",
      "risk": "systemConfiguration", "valueBasis": "documented", "activation": "reboot",
      "limitations": "On by default (no value is stored): on a PC nobody tweaked, nothing changes. Where the value is 0, Mesura sets it to 1 (on).",
      "source": "Microsoft Learn 'Introduction to Threaded DPCs' (enabled by default; ThreadDpcEnable set to zero disables them; the page writes the key as SessionManager\\Kernel). The Registry Tweaks corpus sets it to 0.",
      "registry": [ { "hive": "HKLM", "path": "SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Session Manager\\kernel", "name": "ThreadDpcEnable", "type": "dword", "value": "1", "absentMatches": true } ]
    },
    {
      "id": "repair.large-system-cache", "name": "Favour programs over the file cache", "category": "Restore Windows defaults",
      "impact": "maintenance", "summary": "Restores Windows' default memory balance.",
      "description": "Sets the memory manager back to favouring programs' working sets (the client default) if a tweak tool set it to favour the file cache, a file-server setting. Restoring the default isn't a performance setting, and no effect is claimed.",
      "risk": "systemConfiguration", "activation": "reboot",
