      "category": "Privacy",
      "impact": "privacy",
      "summary": "Windows no longer connects to the OneSettings service for configuration data.",
      "description": "Sets the Group Policy 'Disable OneSettings Downloads'. Microsoft describes OneSettings as a service Windows components and apps, such as the telemetry service, use to dynamically update their configuration. With the policy on, Windows doesn't attempt to connect to it; otherwise Windows periodically connects to download configuration settings.",
      "risk": "systemConfiguration",
      "level": "moderate",
      "benefit": "documented",
      "valueBasis": "documented",
